<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30467" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nātīvĭtas</span></b> ,
			ātis, f.
		nativus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>birth, nativity</i> (post-class.; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ortus): municipem aut nativitas aut adoptio
					facit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					50, 1, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">janua nativitatis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Anim. 39</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vultum nativitatis,</span>”
				<i>natural face</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Jacob. 1, 23</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(b).</b>
			<i>Plur.</i>, <i><span class="en">Tert. Spect.
			30</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>A generation</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">usque ad quartam nativitatem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Marc. 4, 27 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
